From b04ea1e959e7fb377614fd1ce9d6003fd10ee0c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:46:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Always use OpenGL stereo output in the GUI

Sparky Stereo OS draws every output through the desktop: a quad-buffered
window is declared to KWin as full side by side, and KWin's output filters
decide what each screen shows. Request stereo buffers always, always use the
OpenGL stereo output whatever is given on the command line, and remove the
output modes from the 3D Modes menu. All input modes stay. Keep the settings
in their own folder, Bino3D-stereo, beside the ones of a stock Bino.

Edition-specific; not meant for upstream as it is.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
